      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Extract **ONLY** the first name from this email address {{ $('Google Sheets3').item.json.emails }} . Follow these steps meticulously:  \n\n1. **Isolate Local Part**:  \n   - Extract text before \"@\".  \n   *Example: `abovethecrowd.john_doe2023@domain.com` \u2192 `abovethecrowd.john_doe2023`*  \n\n2. **Split Segments**:  \n   - Split using delimiters: `. - _ 0-9 +`  \n   - **CamelCase Handling**: Split uppercase letters (e.g., `JohnDoe` \u2192 `[\"John\", \"Doe\"]`).  \n\n3. **Blocklist Filtering** (case-insensitive):  \n   - Reject segments matching:  \n     `info, admin, support, contact, mail, sales, hello, team, realestate, office, hr, noreply, marketing, service, make, above, crowd, property, homes, listings, agent, properties, management, realty, biz, corporate, help, inquiry`  \n4. **Validation**:  \n   - Starts with `A-Z`  \n   - Length: `2-12 letters`  \n   - No numbers/special characters  \n   - **Name Check**: Must match common first names (e.g., \"John\", \"Sarah\", NOT \"Service\" or \"AboveTheCrowd\").  \n\n5. **Select & Format**:  \n   - Take the **first valid segment**.  \n   - Format: `Proper Case` (e.g., `JOHN` \u2192 `John`).  \n\n6. **Fallback**:  \n   - If no valid segments, return `\"there\"`.  \n\n**Return ONLY the name or \"there\" with no extra text.**  \n\n---  \n\n### **Examples**  \n| Email Address                  | Output  |  \n|--------------------------------|---------|  \n| `service.michael@domain.com`   | Michael |  \n| `AboveTheCrowd@domain.com`     | there   |  \n| `AgentSarahL@domain.com`       | Sarah   |  \n| `JohnDoe2023@domain.com`       | John    |  \n| `Corporate.Help@domain.com`    | there   |  \n\n**No explanations. Only the result.**  "
